       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as up to 850 mg three times daily. For extended-release it is 2,000 to 2,550 mg/day. This dose is twice that maximum, and it risks lactic acidosis and GI toxicity even with normal kidney function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I may still not be able to enter it as written."
